A||||4||sqoach||Uneven idle after start-up (read: when cold)||||1||
Z||000000||sqoach||09-17-2001||02:55 PM||||After I start my car (86 V6 4spd) the idle "searches." At first it's idling around 1500, then it will go down below 700 and kick back up to 1500. It does this for about two minutes, then it slowly goes down to 1000 and pretty much stays. Should I check my IAC? I don't know much about the V6's, this is my first one. Maybe a vaccuum leak? There sure is a bunch of those vaccuum lines.<BR>Also, not sure if this is related, but when I first start my car when it hasn't been starting for a few hours, it starts just fine. But when it's warmed up, it doesn't seem to start as easy. Takes a few more cranks.<P>Ideas much appreciated.<P>------------------<BR>-Adam<BR><FONT COLOR="BLUE">sqoach@yahoo.com</FONT><BR>           <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach.gif">       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/halfpole.gif">           <BR>^^^^^^<B>new project</B>^^^^^^<BR><LI><FONT SIZE="1">84 SE (FOR SALE)*SOLD(?)*<BR><LI>85 Coupe (parts car)($50)*sale pending*<BR><LI>86 SC</FONT><p>[This message has been edited by sqoach (edited 09-17-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||SLYGUY||09-18-2001||03:32 AM||||Did you run a diagnostic of the ECU? When I did that it came back as an faulty EGR valve. If you don't have a Haynes Fiero book...GET ONE. <P>In the troubleshooting section it describes the very symptom you are and states that it is the EGR. I'm gonna replace mine tomorrow because my 88GT searches for an idle too.<P>Sly||||reg||1
Z||000002||falconhulk||09-18-2001||08:15 AM||||The egr valve is not functioniong when the car is at idle.  It could be stuck partially open though.  i had a problem with my car stalling on slow down so I disconnected and plugged the EGR vacuum line.  For some strange reason now my car idles at 1500 when its cold but slowly goes to 1000.  It does not search like yours does but it is similar.  This is also only in park as when its in drive the idle does to 1000 right away even if it is at 1500 when I shift to drive.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/i-4_b_l.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||btoth||09-18-2001||12:16 PM||||I do believe it's normal for it to idle at 1500 when cold.  (Even my new engine does it.)  Once warm (after about 2 min) it drops to 900/800RPM and idles perfectly.<P>If it's doing a lot of hunting something is probably screwy.  Did you give it a tune-up?  Maybe you could try reseting the computer. Maybe it had "learned" something at some point and is compensating for a bad sensor or something.  And just to eliminate it as a possibility - check where the timing is set to.  How many miles are on the engine?<P>BTW - it wouldn't hurt to replace the EGR valve... it's cheap and they're a common thing to replace it seems.  Just make sure to get an AC Delco replacement.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by btoth (edited 09-18-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||sqoach||09-18-2001||05:33 PM||||I don't have any codes. I'm pretty sure it's been doing this ever since I got it. (over 2 months ago) It doesn't do this for very long. I had someone check the timing for me. 82K miles. I thought EGR valves were expensive? Where did I hear that? What all should I do for a tune-up? I've done a few things already. Do you have a list I can follow?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
